From 8a5af2fe795295ad768e63c72989319fd0b2ad14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:03:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 25/25] hw/avr, hw/ssi, hw/timer, hw/misc: Nano Base Click
 slots, 8x8 G Click

- avr8x-spi: AVR8X SPI host (normal and buffered mode flags, DORD), on an
  SSI bus "spi0.spi".
- avr8x-tcb: TCB periodic interrupt mode on QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL from
  CLK_PER (DIV1/DIV2), CAPT interrupt, CNT, STATUS.RUN.
- max7219: MAX7219 LED driver chain on SSI, LOAD latches; decode, scan
  limit, shutdown, display test; "display" and "intensity" properties.
- mikrobus: the Click catalog and plugging code shared by all boards
  (from the MC00 machine, which now uses it): a board describes its
  sockets (pads behind RST/PWM/INT/CS, I2C and SPI buses). New Click:
  8x8g (MAX7219 on SPI, LOAD on CS). Click parts build with CONFIG_MIKROBUS.
- avr64ea48-cnano: mb1=, mb2=, mb3= plug Clicks into the three mikroBUS
  sockets of a Curiosity Nano Base for Click boards (AC164162), with the
  pins of its user guide and the Nano's edge pins.
- qtests: SPI to the 8x8 G Click, TCB period and flag; board docs.

firmware/avr-hello's matrix demo shows its frames on the twin and prints
the same VCOM transcript as the kit.

Peripheral Pretender: AI-assisted, not for upstream QEMU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
