@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+Microchip AVR64EA48 Curiosity Nano (``avr64ea48-cnano``)
+========================================================
+
+.. note::
+   Peripheral Pretender: a personal project in a downstream fork
+   of QEMU. AI-assisted code; not for submission to upstream QEMU.
+
+The AVR64EA48 Curiosity Nano evaluation kit (EV66E56A) carries an
+AVR64EA48: an AVRxt core with 64 KiB of flash, 6 KiB of SRAM and 512 bytes
+of EEPROM. It runs at OSCHF 20 MHz / 6 after reset.
+
+CPU: ``avrxt`` (target/avr). The register file is not in the data space,
+I/O starts at data address 0, and interrupts follow CPUINT (two levels,
+LVL1VEC, LVL0PRI with round robin, IVSEL). ELF files built by avr-gcc for
+avrxmega2..7 are accepted.
+
+The SoC model (``avr64ea48-soc``, generic ``avr8x-soc``) is built from the
+device description generated from the AVR64EA48 ATDF (AVR-Ex DFP 2.8.189)
+and ``profiles/avr64ea48.yaml`` of Peripheral Pretender. Modelled: PORT and
+VPORT (``/machine/soc/port``, ``pa-levels``..``pf-levels``,
+``pa-stats``..), USART (asynchronous), SPI (host), TCB (periodic
+interrupt), CLKCTRL, CPUINT, NVMCTRL (FLMAP only; commands are logged),
+SIGROW, SYSCFG.REVID (``silicon-rev`` B1 = 0x21), USERROW, FUSE, LOCK.
+Every other instance is a generic register block that logs writes with
+``-d unimp``.
+
+Board: LED0 on PB3 (active low), SW0 on PB2 (``-M avr64ea48-cnano,
+sw0-pressed=on``), the virtual COM port on USART1 (``-serial`` 0), USART2
+on ``-serial`` 1.
+
+On a Curiosity Nano Base for Click boards (AC164162), ``mb1=``, ``mb2=``
+and ``mb3=`` plug a Click board into mikroBUS socket 1-3 (``thermo8`` needs
+I2C, which is not modelled yet; ``buttong``, ``7seg``, ``relay`` and
+``8x8g``, a MAX7219 LED matrix with a ``display`` property, work). The
+Click is ``/machine/mbN-click``.
+
+Firmware comes from ``-kernel`` or ``-bios``::
+
+    qemu-system-avr -M avr64ea48-cnano,mb1=8x8g -kernel matrix.elf \
+        -display none -serial stdio -d unimp,guest_errors
